WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.919 --> 00:00:05.330
In Game of Thrones, Sansa Stark has a pretty
rough relationship history.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:09.040
She’s betrothed to Prince Joffrey, and he
turns out to be a psycho.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:13.080
Then briefly there’s a plan to marry her
to a Tyrell – Loras in the show and Willas

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.949
in the books – but the Lannisters find out
the plan and quickly marry Sansa to Tyrion

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:20.090
– who is then sentenced to death and flees
the country.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:24.911
In the show, Sansa then goes north and marries
Ramsay, the worst psycho of all, though in

00:00:24.911 --> 00:00:29.280
the books she instead goes to the Vale and
is promised to a guy called Harry Hardyng

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:33.609
. Harry’s kind of a douche , but he is the
heir the Vale – marrying him could make

00:00:33.609 --> 00:00:37.940
Sansa very powerful . So will Sansa settle
down with this guy?

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:38.940
Maybe not.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.789
There’s some really interesting evidence
in the books that Sansa may have one more

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:44.249
suitor.

00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:48.359
Game of Thrones author George Martin has written
some prequel stories set a hundred years before

00:00:48.359 --> 00:00:52.379
the main series, about the adventures of the
characters Dunk and Egg.

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:56.010
In the first of these stories, Dunk and Egg
go to a tournament at Ashford.

00:00:56.010 --> 00:01:00.199
In the tournament, combatants fight to be
named one of five champions of the young Lady

00:01:00.199 --> 00:01:01.199
Ashford.

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:06.509
The final five champions, in order, are Lyonel
Baratheon, Tybolt Lannister, Leo Tyrell, Humfrey

00:01:06.509 --> 00:01:08.840
Hardyng, and Valarr Targaryen.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.200
Which just happens to almost perfectly line
up with the men Sansa’s married or been

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.740
promised to – a Baratheon, a Tyrell, a Lannister,
and a Hardyng.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:21.750
There are complications – the Ashford Tyrell
and Lannister aren’t quite in the right

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:26.340
order, Lyonel might actually be second, and
Joffrey isn’t a true Baratheon – he’s

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.670
a Lannister who people think is a Baratheon.

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:32.650
But still, this pattern lines up too well
to be a coincidence – especially given the

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:36.240
inclusion of House Hardyng, which is a pretty
obscure house.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:39.850
So the point is that the Ashford champions
seem to seem to predict Sansa’s suitors

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:44.920
– and since the fifth champion is Valarr
Targaryen, it seems that Sansa will marry

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.490
or be promised to a Targaryen.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.140
So who could this be?

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:54.200
After Robert’s Rebellion – and the deaths
of the Mad King, and Prince Rhaegar, and later

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.250
Viserys, Daenerys seems to be the last of
the Targaryens, and unless Westeros introduces

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.829
gay marriage, Sansa, sadly, probably won’t
hook up with her.

00:02:02.829 --> 00:02:05.920
But there actually are other living Targaryens.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.799
At the end of Season 6, we learn that Jon
Snow is the son of Ned Stark’s sister Lyanna

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:16.290
and Dany’s dead brother Rhaegar, meaning
that Jon is a Targaryen – so maybe Sansa

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.909
will marry him.

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:21.580
This could make sense politically – as the
son of Prince Rhaegar, Jon could make a claim

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.959
on the Iron Throne, as King of Westeros, and
marriage to Sansa could win him the support

00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:27.019
of the north.

00:02:27.019 --> 00:02:31.129
In the show, Jon already rules the north,
but he’s in a weird tension with Sansa created

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:34.910
by Littlefinger – maybe marriage could settle
that conflict.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:39.170
So in the both books and show the politics
probably could work, the tricky question is

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:41.400
how this would work on a personal level.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.260
Jon and Sansa are cousins, and it’s not
unusual for people in Westeros to marry their

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:50.380
cousins – for example Tywin Lannister married
his cousin – but Jon and Sansa grew up thinking

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:54.730
they were siblings, or half-siblings, cause
Jon was believed Ned’s bastard.

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.769
They were never very close – Jon and Sansa
don’t have a single conversation in any

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:03.090
of the books – but still, they think of
each other as brother and sister , so it does

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.180
feel pretty gross for them to get together.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.310
But would that stop George Martin?

00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:12.049
In an early outline of Game of Thrones, Martin
had Jon and Arya falling in love, so he has

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:15.370
considered Snow on Stark romance before.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:18.930
Also for what it’s worth we do know Jon
likes redheads.

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.920
So it could go either way – maybe Sansa
will marry Jon.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.640
But there is another possibility, because
Jon isn’t Rhaegar Targaryen’s only child.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:32.269
With his wife Elia, Rhaegar had a daughter
called Rhaenys, and a son called Aegon.

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:36.250
We’re told that these kids were killed by
Gregor Clegane in Robert’s Rebellion – but

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:41.049
in the books, Varys claims to have saved Aegon
and to’ve secretly raised him to be a perfect

00:03:41.049 --> 00:03:45.610
king, and in Book 5, Aegon begins an invasion
of Westeros.

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:50.599
Popular theories suggest that this Aegon is
a fake, no true Targaryen at all – check

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:55.300
out the Varys video for details – but Aegon
could probably still fit this Ashford pattern,

00:03:55.300 --> 00:03:59.130
because, well, Joffrey isn’t a true Baratheon
but he still seems to fit.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:01.959
So could Aegon be the Targaryen Sansa marries?

00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:07.000
Again, the politics could work – to take
over Westeros, Aegon needs allies, and Sansa’s

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.480
the “key to the north” . This could possibly
also work romantically – Sansa and Aegon

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.349
are both young, pretty, and basically decent
people, so it’s easy enough to imagine them

00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:16.349
falling in love.

00:04:16.349 --> 00:04:20.300
It could also fit nicely with the prophecy
of a “younger and more beautiful” queen

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:25.520
coming to cast down Cersei Lannister – Sansa
could become that queen.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.240
So there are points on both sides.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:32.060
Maybe Sansa will marry her cousin Jon Targaryen,
or maybe she’ll marry Aegon Targaryen.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.600
Or maybe this pattern means nothing and she’ll
marry someone else, or no one at all.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:40.080
It’s too early to know for sure, but after
Sansa’s history of evil exes, you can only

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.620
hope she’ll end up with someone she likes.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:43.690
Thanks for watching.

00:04:43.690 --> 00:04:47.520
If you want to know more about Jon’s parents,
or about Varys and Aegon, check out the video

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.750
links in the description.

00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:52.500
Also, if you haven’t read Dunk and Egg,
the Game of Thrones prequel stories, you might

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:55.750
want to check them out – they’re much
shorter and lighter than the main Thrones

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:58.150
series, and well worth a read if you’re
a fan.

